  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/sim_tool_body.rs`: the viewport simulation draws a drawn (spun) holder with its own outline (`SpunProfile::outline`). Tapers and arcs show as drawn. Before, it showed the stepped bands that the collision laws read.\n- With a drawn holder, the simulation also draws the shank as stored. The judged record widens the shank to each band that touches the shank top (`HolderProfile::enclose`). Before, a Ø44 holder foot made the shank look Ø44 down to the flutes.\n- New `JudgedOutline::with_drawn(drawn, stored)`. It refuses (`OutlineError::PastJudged`) a drawn point outside every band at its height, and a stored cutter that is wider or longer than the judged one. The picture is never wider than the check.\n- A machine-default holder (#828) and an imported STL/STEP body keep the band drawing.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2176-sim-draws-drawn-holder.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The trace is on the issue. All consumers already read one landed body: the collision checks, the verify/post gate (`kept_rejudge` -> `collect_job` -> `job_tool`) and the simulation. Only the picture was wrong. The issue stays P3.\n- Posted G-code and the check results do not change for existing projects. Only the display changes. The checks still read the bands and the widened shank. These are never smaller than the drawn shape.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/sim_tool_drawn_holder.rs`:\n- `a_drawn_holder_is_drawn_with_its_own_radii_and_lengths` (the profile of the issue picture)\n- `a_drawn_cone_is_drawn_as_a_cone_and_judged_as_its_enclosing_band` (moved from `sim_tool_body.rs`, where it pinned the old band drawing; the test count stays the same)\n- `a_profile_edit_redraws_the_holder_and_undo_restores_it`\n- `checks_verify_and_simulation_read_one_holder_shape`\n\nQuick gate (debug, `-j 6`): `sim_tool_drawn_holder` 4/4, `sim_tool_body` 6/6, `tool_body_judged` 8/8, `tool_neck_laws` 4/4, `tool_spun_profile` 7/7, `holder_library` 12/12. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The `camcraft-ui` crate was not built or tested. Its sim test (`egui_app/tests/tool_body.rs`) uses an imported STL body, which keeps the band drawing. No public item that it uses changed.\n- No GUI screenshot. The change is in the tool-frame mesh only.\n- A spun body with `machine_default` set is not pinned. It keeps the old path.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe judged shank is widened by a band that only touches the shank top (`reach_over` uses inclusive bounds). That can be over-conservative for the shank laws. This PR does not change any law.\n\nChangelog: The simulation now draws a drawn tool holder with its own profile (tapers and arcs), and the shank with its stored diameter, in place of stepped cylinders.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2176\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
